    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47973" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεᾱτ-ής</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεητής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεάομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who
			sees</i> or <i>goes to see</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς χώρης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.139
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				301
			</span></i>; in the theatre, <i>spectator</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				575
			</span></i>, al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. σοφιστῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.38
				</span></i>
			; <i>one who contemplates</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τἀληθοῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1098a31
				</span></i>
			.</div>
